IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `carer-types`

-- Carer Recognition Act 2010 (Cth) — THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
-- The carer asks: "Am I a carer under this Act; what must the agency do; can
-- I enforce it?"

§ `Rules`

-- s 5(1): "a carer is an individual who provides personal care, support and
-- assistance to another individual who needs it because that other
-- individual: (a) has a disability; or (b) has a medical condition
-- (including a terminal or chronic illness); or (c) has a mental illness; or
-- (d) is frail and aged." (2): not under a contract, as voluntary work for an
-- organisation, or as part of a course. (3): not merely because a relative,
-- guardian or co-resident.
@ref s 5
@export Am I a carer under s 5 of the Carer Recognition Act 2010 (Cth)? Yes if I give personal care, support and assistance to another individual who needs it because of a disability, a medical condition (including a terminal or chronic illness), a mental illness, or being frail and aged; but not where I give it under a contract, as voluntary work for a charitable, welfare or community organisation, or as part of a course of education or training. Being a relative, guardian or housemate is not enough by itself. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Carer case`  @desc The care I give, why it is needed, and on what basis
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am a carer under the Act` c IF
        c's `I provide personal care, support and assistance`
    AND NOT (c's `the need` EQUALS `none of these`)
    AND c's `the basis` EQUALS `informally`

-- s 7(1): each public service agency must take all practicable measures for
-- its staff and agents to be aware of and understand the Statement; s 9(a):
-- likewise each associated provider.
@ref ss 7(1), 9(a)
GIVEN c IS A `Carer case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body must make its staff aware of the Statement for` c IF
    NOT (c's `the body I deal with` EQUALS `another body`)

-- s 8(1): a public service care agency must take all practicable measures to
-- reflect the Statement's principles in care supports; s 9(b): likewise an
-- associated provider.
@ref ss 8(1), 9(b)
GIVEN c IS A `Carer case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body must reflect the Statement in care supports for` c IF
        c's `the body I deal with` EQUALS `a public service care agency`
    OR  c's `the body I deal with` EQUALS `an associated provider`

-- s 8(2): "Each public service care agency is to consult carers, or bodies
-- that represent carers, when developing or evaluating care supports."
@ref s 8(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Carer case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body must consult carers for` c IF
    c's `the body I deal with` EQUALS `a public service care agency`

§ `The top-level goal`

-- s 10(1): "This Act does not create rights or duties that are legally
-- enforceable in judicial or other proceedings." (2): "A failure to comply
-- with this Act does not affect the validity of any decision, and is not a
-- ground for the review or challenge of any decision."
@ref ss 5, 7-10
@export default The carer's position under the Carer Recognition Act 2010 (Cth): whether I am a carer (s 5); whether the body I deal with must make its staff aware of the Statement for Australia's Carers (ss 7(1), 9(a)), reflect its principles in care supports (ss 8(1), 9(b)) and consult carers on care supports (s 8(2)); and that none of this is legally enforceable, nor a ground to challenge a decision (s 10). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Carer case`  @desc The care I give, why it is needed, the basis, and the body I deal with
GIVETH A `Carer position`
`the carer position for` c MEANS
    `Carer position` WITH
        `I am a carer`                                  IS `I am a carer under the Act` c
        `the body must make its staff aware of the Statement` IS `the body must make its staff aware of the Statement for` c
        `the body must reflect the Statement in care supports` IS `the body must reflect the Statement in care supports for` c
        `the body must consult carers on care supports` IS `the body must consult carers for` c
        `I can enforce these obligations`               IS FALSE
        `non-compliance invalidates a decision`         IS FALSE
